[quote="Powerhound_2000"]

Not as bad as the Ennead since there is an alernate win condition but advanced Gloomweaver against&nbsp;Legacy, The Wraith, and Parse in Megalopolis leaves you with a long game. &nbsp;As it leaves you only with the option of taking out his relics or letting him flip. &nbsp;

[/quote]
Which, if one of the Relics is eaten by the Final Wasteland while Unforgiving Wasteland is in play, becomes rather... difficult. &nbsp;This scenario is technically still winnable, because the Mongolian Death Worm deals the highest HP target 3 Toxic Damage. &nbsp;But it would take a very, very long time. &nbsp;And if the Mongolian Death Worm is taken out by the Horrid Skunk-Ape, then it too would be lost and the game would become unwinnable.

&nbsp;

Careful managing could in theory cause every target besides the Horrid Skunk-Ape, the heroes, and Gloomy to be lost in the Final Wasteland. &nbsp;This would leave Gloomweaver playing nothing but Vast Followings and Strenght of the Grave, and the environment having nothing but Con&#39;s Bunker, Unforgiving Wasteland, Ancient Library, and the last Horrid Skunk-Ape, leaving the game in an infinite unending limbo as the heroes fight on forever, unable to harm Gloomweaver but unwilling to surrender what remains of our once beautiful planet into his hands.
